es.","31…Nxe5 wins a pawn and threatens …Nf3+, winning a rook, picking it up with 33…Nxd2+.","Takes the e5 pawn and wins a pawn once the captures settle."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"31…Nxe5!! ignores the attack on the knight on f4 and takes the e5 pawn first. Taking the knight gives Black the material back and more."},{"title":"What Black gives up","text":"The knight on f4 is attacked by the g3 pawn, and 31…Nxe5 doesn't save it. That's a knight on offer."},{"title":"If White takes the knight","text":"32.gxf4 is met by 32…Nf3+, and the knight on e5 gets away. Then 33…Nxd2+ gives check, and 34…Rxc2 takes the bishop on c2. Black ends up a piece ahead: Black is winning (−6.21)."},{"title":"White's best try","text":"White's best is to leave the knight alone and play 32.Bd1. Black answers 32…Nd5, and the knight on f4 gets away, planting the knight on the d5 outpost. Then 33…Rc1+ gives check, and 34…Rc2 threatens …Rxe2, winning a bishop. Black ends up a pawn ahead: Black is clearly better (−1.96)."},{"title":"Why not save the knight first?","text":"Saving it with 31…Nd5, the best way to do that, is clearly weaker (+0.26 against −1.96). White answers 32.f4, threatening Nd6, winning a knight. That would leave Black level."}]},{"ply":64,"name":"32…Nd5","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"32…Nd5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Plants the knight on d5: a pawn defends it and no enemy pawn can chase it away.","Moves the attacked knight to safety.","The next best move, 32…Nc4, would drop Black's winning chances from 69% to 57% (−0.79).","32…Nd5 gets the knight out of the way of gxf4.","White was threatening gxf4, winning a knight. The knight steps away.","White answers 33.Be2, leaving Black with a king with pawns missing from its shelter."]}],"opening":{"name":"Ruy Lopez: Closed, Pilnik Variation","eco":"C90","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 11…cxd4: 22 moves in all, 11 by White and 11 by Black.","Theory runs out after 11…cxd4: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}